==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|часъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|часъ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*časъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-час.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-час.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|as|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|c|par=+|loc=+|pauc=часа́|adj=часово́й|dim=ча́сик,часо́к}}

# {{lb|ru|in the singular}} [[hour]], [[o'clock]], [[time]], time of day
#: {{uxi|ru|Кото́рый '''час'''?|What '''time''' is it?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|В кото́ром '''часу́'''?|At what '''time'''?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''час'''|'''one o’clock'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''час''' но́чи|one '''a.m.'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|в '''час'''|at '''one o’clock'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|до '''ча́су'''|until '''one o’clock'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|оди́н '''час'''|one '''hour'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|два '''часа́'''|two '''o’clock'''; two '''hours'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|в два '''часа́'''|at two '''o’clock'''}}
# {{lb|ru|in the plural}} [[hours]], [[o'clock]]
#: {{coi|ru|[[че́тверть]] '''ча́са'''|a [[quarter of an hour|quarter of an '''hour''']], [[quarter-hour|quarter-'''hour''']]}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[полтора́]] '''часа́'''|an '''hour''' and a half}}
#: {{uxi|ru|пять '''часо́в'''|five '''o’clock'''; five '''hours'''}}
# {{lb|ru|in the plural}} [[clock]], [[watch]]
#: {{uxi|ru|на мои́х '''часа́х'''|by my '''watch'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|У моего́ бра́та не́сколько '''часо́в'''.|My brother has several '''watches'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|Э́ти '''часы́''' не иду́т.|This '''clock/watch''' doesn’t work.}}
# {{lb|ru|poetic}} [[time]], [[day]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Час''' распла́ты наста́л.|The day of reckoning has arrived.}}

====Usage notes====
* After numbers in the nominative/accusative case that govern genitive singular nouns (those ending in 2, 3 or 4, but not those ending in 12, 13 or 14), the stress of the genitive singular moves to the last syllable: {{m|ru|[[два]] '''часа́'''}}, {{m|ru|[[двадцать|два́дцать]] [[три]] '''часа́'''}}, {{m|ru|[[сорок|со́рок]] [[четыре|четы́ре]] '''часа́'''}}.

